Found by the bob-cli-oe land agent while verifying bob-cli-oe.2 (bob-plugins master 570c3a10).

`successorShakeRow` in `plugins/bob-navigation-hotkeys/src/206d-*.js` starts with:

```js
if (!modal || !modal.resultsEl || typeof modal.resultsEl.querySelector === "function") {
  return;
}
```

The guard is inverted: in a real DOM `querySelector` is a function, so the helper always returns before adding `is-shake`. The callers in 206c (verdict refusals, around line 520) and 206e (Ctrl+J jump refusal, around lines 369-376) also shake before the modal's full re-render, which would replace the shaken row element anyway. To reproduce: open the successor card on a model with a muted row, highlight it, and press Ctrl+X (or Ctrl+J). The refusal status line appears but the row never shakes. It has been broken since 8a16ebea (2026-11-05).
